```
    elif _equal(a, b):
        return
    else:
        ops.append(...)
```

Wait, but containers of the same kind that are equal descend and produce nothing — no problem. Non-container pairs (scalars, or dict vs list, dict vs scalar, etc.) that are equal — only scalars can be equal (a dict can't equal a list in _equal since their types differ). So `elif _equal(a,b): return` catches equal scalars. Type-mismatched dict vs list → falls through to else → `~`. Correct.
